  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1135 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThere is no real relief from the unseasonable heat in sight, with\nwidespread triple digit highs expected to persist through at least\nmuch of next week. Heat headlines will be needed for most if not\nall of the forecast area from Saturday into next week, and a few\nspots may see heat index values peak near or just above 110 \ndegrees on some afternoons. Isolated diurnal showers or \nthunderstorms may occur just about any afternoon Saturday through \nearly next week, especially over the higher terrain areas, but any\nrainfall will be brief and only provide temporary heat relief. \nGusty winds will be possible with any storm that may occur. The \nrain chances at any one location remain below mentionable levels \nat this time. Record or near record high temperatures will be \nlikely much of next week.",
